Yes. The Matelas Hybride comes with a 10-year full warranty for the original purchaser when bought directly from Tediber or an authorised Tediber boutique.
It covers, in particular:
visible sagging of more than 2.5 cm;
a physical defect causing significant cracking or deformation during normal use;
manufacturing defects in the cover;
persistent rubbing noises coming from inside the mattress.
If the defect is confirmed and eligible, Tediber provides a repair or replacement. Delivery is covered, and reasonable return costs may be reimbursed with proof. The warranty does not provide a refund.
It excludes normal wear, normal loss of firmness, stains, tears, moisture or mould, personal comfort preferences, and mattresses not unpacked within 30 days of delivery. To make a claim, send a clear description, photos of the issue and proof of purchase to hello@tediber.com.

yuma-tediber-shopping-2026-10-08|compare.a:
Honestly, if your budget is tight, the Hybride is the smarter buy. It already gives you the core benefits: pocket springs, 7 comfort layers, stable support, and a semi-firm feel. You are not settling for a basic mattress.
The Hybride Premium is worth the extra only if you specifically want:
a more cushioned, balanced feel;
2 additional centimetres and one extra comfort layer;
thicker foam for more precise support;
a reversible comfort layer, with a softer or firmer side;
better movement absorption if you sleep with a partner.
So my honest recommendation for you is: choose the Hybride. Choose the Premium only if one of those comfort features is important enough to justify the additional cost. Both are designed as substantial hybrid mattresses, but the Premium is an upgrade in comfort and adjustability, not a completely different level of product.

